1 Installation
**************

Dicom.el is available from ELPA
(https://elpa.gnu.org/packages/dicom.html) or MELPA
(https://melpa.org/#/dicom) and can be installed via ‘M-x
package-install RET dicom RET’.  After installation, you can open
‘DICOMDIR’ and DICOM image files.

   Emacs must be compiled with support for PNG, SVG and XML.  The
package relies on external programs from the DCMTK
(https://dcmtk.org/en/dcmtk/) DICOM toolkit, which is widely available
on Linux distributions.

   • ‘dcm2xml’ and ‘dcm2img’ from the DCMTK
     (https://dcmtk.org/en/dcmtk/) DICOM toolkit
   • ‘magick’ from ImageMagick (https://imagemagick.org/)
   • ‘ffmpeg’ for video conversion (optional)
   • ‘mpv’ for video playing (optional)


